    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: return `membershipTier: 'SILVER'` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `'BRONZE'`.\n\nBoth inputs \u2014 `namesakeCount` and `email` \u2014 already live on `Owner`, and the codebase already exposes read-only derived attributes (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`) as plain getters that Jackson serializes. So the tier belongs there as a single-responsibility derived getter, reusing that established pattern rather than adding logic to the controller or service.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getMembershipTier()`: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-empty, else `BRONZE` (null-safe on both fields).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 documented the new read-only `membershipTier` property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) alongside the sibling derived fields, keeping the spec in sync with the model.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass with no regressions.",
